un `39247424292`. Do not repeat those edits in ATK. Coordinator evidence acquisition remains the route for any genuinely missing companion material.\n- Source publication does not establish installation, live discovery recovery or visual acceptance. Preserve the reported five failed diagnostic images as failures. The prerequisite catalogue’s open PR #9 establishes no merge proof or new dependency; legacy migration satisfies none.\n- The coordinator continues monitoring every qualifying PR and repair successor through successful `dev` merge and required post-merge repair. Include `self_host` only for GitHub-agent functionality.\n- Retain ten workers, truthful labels including `agent:writing`, independent resolver-mediated choices, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with complete Q&A, waiting-agent recovery, and singleton 30-minute orchestration while relevant PRs are open, with idle exit.\n- Restrict notifications to user approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. This correction grants no hold release, main promotion or runtime activation and does not declare #9 or the broader objective complete.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"d9c24a19fb48e0b69d3752a8bb1a84a671014cdf59a216f376bc6d1b4e444140","text":"# Repair PR #40’s lint failure while preserving resumable review\n\n## Summary\n\nApply the resolver-selected formatting correction to head `517c7926e4c73592310663d38337bdff7e632656`, against pinned dev `4a17e91b20b2683aca365f486e6217a141ef8c5b`.\n\nComplete assigned feedback and failed-job logs identify E501, PT006 and FORMAT findings in one test module. Python matrix and SDK checks passed; independent source review remains in progress. No files were edited or candidate programs executed during planning.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/repository/github_agent_readonly_preparation.py`, wrap the long assertion verifying that read-only preparation creates no source-review assignment.\n- Replace `\"kind, protocol\"` with `(\"kind\", \"protocol\")` in the unsupported-protocol parametrization. Retain all three existing cases and their values.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting within that module, preserving every assertion, fixture, test name and behavior.\n- Add a concise repair entry under `Unreleased` in `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, preserving history and package versions.\n- Preserve the complete PR feature: resumable independent review, durable merge exclusion, structured scene findings and recoverable publication. Retain the readiness tests, explicit correction fixture and current-dev safeguards.\n- No public APIs, controller interfaces, schemas, dependencies, workflows, compatibility floors or quality baselines change in this correction.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; Pi workers execute no programs, imports, tests, installs, builds or scenes.\n\n- Verify Ruff lint and format checks report no new findings without changing baselines or suppressions.\n- Run the affected preparation module: held planning preserves context and authority; default and typed prompts retain pending assignments; unsupported protocols create neither context nor authority.\n- Run neighboring readiness, source-review and repair-discovery tests. Preserve healthy-baseline blocking cases, integration-nonblocking behavior, checked-renewal/correction/hold coexistence and terminal-publication recovery.\n- Require the resulting exact head to pass Python 3.9–3.14, `py39-min` including `pip check`, both SDK profiles, quality/type/coverage/artifact gates and aggregate ordinary `fast-checks`. Earlier results do not validate changed bytes.\n- Use existing regression suites; no additional tests are needed for this formatting-only correction.\n\n## Review, publication and standing obligations\n\n- Refresh actual head, dev base and writer ownership before editing. Obtain separate independent complete plan review; material changes require renewed review.\n- Publish through the existing signed correction lifecycle, preserving complete chronological task context, Q&A, resolver decisions, plans, checkpoints and source generations.\n- Obtain fresh independent exact-head source, companion and whole-task assessment. Preserve signature, provenance, credential, ownership, veto/cancel, hold and protected exact-head approval gates. Resolver selection approves only the strategy.\n- Retain companion publication `4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0` and its exact-commit CI evidence. Do not repeat its edits in ATK; coordinator evidence acquisition remains responsible for missing companion material. Publication does not establish runtime activation or live recovery.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and repairs until every qualifying PR and repair successor successfully merges into dev. Include self_host changes only when they affect GitHub-agent functionality.\n- Preserve ten workers, truthful labels including `agent:writing`, resolver-mediated choices, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with complete Q&A, waiting-agent recovery and singleton 30-minute orchestration with idle exit.\n- Restrict notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. This correction grants no main/runtime authority, releases no unrelated hold and establishes no completion of #9 or the broader task.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","questions":[{"answer_index":18,"id":"aa1bc3e0576cfbbd385e0474bf6d73d151ed7d3c1d4f5a16d73c56958efd02a9","text":"Planning remains blocked by the source assignment. The assigned repository is `analytics_toolkit`; `self_host` source and its immutable current dev base are unavailable. No files changed or programs executed.\n\nI read all bound current-head check and feedback pages. PR #40’s fast checks succeed; independent review remains rejected and incomplete. The later routing decision does not prove provisioning occurred.\n\n1. **Coordinator:** Can you complete the already-selected `Karapsin/self_host` assignment and expose its source, immutable current dev base, and repository instructions for fresh planning and separate independent plan review?\n\nThe retained correction covers the relevance inventory, independent discovery cases, rename and scheduling regressions, README maintenance guidance, and task changelog fragment. Preserve PR #40’s feature/readiness changes and all standing monitoring and approval requirements. No additional owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"e53beb7b0408674c7febf3578919a9864c98fe8835f00285c695d438484d0e05","text":"1. Should the revised correction reconcile PR #40 with pinned dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9, preserving newer dev safeguards—including visual-renderer protected approval and rename coverage—alongside the existing resumable-review feature and readiness tests, then obtain separate independent plan review?\nReconcile dev (Recommended): Retain current dev behavior and PR #40’s intended additions; review material conflicts independently and validate the resulting exact head on GitHub."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that","task_id":"68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","version":2}